        {
          "id": 2570678503,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Hi John,\nThe associated EI for ICMP_TIMXCEED was:\n\"Type indicates an error\", which is likely redundant to many users as the string this icmp-type is bound to is \"Time-to-live exceeded\", which adequately describes its meaning.\n\nThe situation is similar for type 39 but on closer inspection I would agree that the previous EI message \"Type is deprecated\" is much more descriptive than what the string this icmp-type is bound to, which is just \"SKIP\"",
          "author": {
            "id": 28545263,
            "username": "1994scm",
